    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but stepping back feels just as exhausting as moving forward. sitting here in the dark doesn't change the fact that the trail is gone. it just feels like everyone else found a way through the fog, and i'm just... stuck at the edge, staring into nothing. it's almost peaceful though, in a weird way. how quiet it is. it's like the world is finally telling me that there's nothing left to do.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
